      "title": "SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Farrell Team Tech Crew (Fall 2026)",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Farrell Team Tech Crew (Fall 2026) SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Farrell Team Tech Crew (Fall 2026) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Farrell Team Tech Crew (Fall 2026) Category: Active Student Jobs Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Farrell Student and Community Center and Campus Events Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Aug 11, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Hourly Salary Type: Hourly Salary Range: $16.00 - $16.00 Position ID: 203589 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi, founded in 1913, is a student-centered college that offers specialized certificates, nationally-recognized associate degree programs, unique baccalaureate degrees and a master's degree in Nursing Education. A targeted expansion of baccalaureate programs through satellite campuses and on-line has led to a record enrollment of more than 3,400 students. A charter member of the State University of New York system, the college is also recognized for forming innovative partnerships that enhance regional economic growth, and for the college's commitment to civic engagement, applied learning, and service-learning. Located in the beautiful foothills of the Catskill Mountains, Delhi and the surrounding area offer outstanding recreational opportunities and small-town charm. Binghamton, the Capitol District and Metropolitan New York are easily accessible. SUNY Delhi was recognized in 2009, 2010 and 2015 as a \"Great College to Work for\" by the Chronicle of Higher Education. Job Description: The Farrell Student & Community Center is looking for students to serve as a member of the Farrell Team Tech Crew.  Reporting to the Director of the Farrell Student & Community Center and Campus Events, members of the Farrell Team Tech Crew largely assist in late night and weekend programming associated with the CSLE Department and Student Senate-funded club and organization events in their audio-visual needs for event held in and near the Farrell Student and Community Center.  Students in the position would work independently or in small groups to work with the program sponsors to ensure events Job duties include, but are not limited to: Provide general A/V technology support for CSLE and/or Student Senate-funded student campus events in the Farrell Student & Community Center. Keep the A/V storage areas and The Okun Theatre Tech Desk and Projection Booth neat and organized Assist in maintaining an updated inventory of supplies Notify the Director of any equipment or repair needs Attend required student employee staff meetings and trainings Other duties as assigned by the Director. Requirements: Applicants must: Have a minimum of a 2.25 GPA Have a clean campus judicial record Be able to work with others in a team Have good verbal and written communication skills Be good problem-solvers and troubleshooters Be available nights and weekends (schedules are varied and hours are sporadic depending on events scheduled and the needs of the sponsors.) Carry a minimum of 12 institutional credits at SUNY Delhi Show proficiency in and/or willingness to learn basic theatre tech equipment. Desired Qualifications: Prior experience with high school theaters or similar.  Proficiency in basic sound reinforcement, microphones, audio cabling, theatre lighting design and usage.  Familiarity with basic video equipment hook ups and computers. Additional Information: This position works in conjunction with the Farrell Building Team Members who work the Information Desk and the Farrell Game Room.  Student Team members will be asked to participate in training sessions throughout the semester.  Farrell Team Tech Crew members can expect, on average, 1-2 hours a week minimum, but can be as much as 6-8 hours per week depending on the events needing coverage,  Hours are mostly night and can include weekends. Application Instructions: Please upload your Co-Curricular Transcript or Resume. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
