d ability of participants so they can meet course objectives Communicate regularly with participants to ensure they are aware of progress Complete records and reports in a timely manner and return then to lesson coordinator Participate in regular in-service training sessions Complete additional duties as assigned by supervisor RESPONSIBLE TO: Swim Lesson Coordinator, Aquatics Director Plans and organizes personal class teaching outlines, methods and goals that support the general teaching outlines provided by the Aquatics Manager *-- Organizes and directs activities of assigned students in order to provide a high level of quality instruction for all students. *-- Insures that all class students are registered, with a registration card prior to beginning class, are thoroughly involved, are on a first-name personalized basis in meaningful instruction for the two-week duration and are in receipt of appropriate certificates and awards as the session concludes. Show up 10 minutes before you start your first class to set up. Enforces pool safety standards and facility operational rules for all individuals using the facilities. Completes and submits records and documentation of completed lessons to the Aquatics Manager Requirements: -- Must be at least 16 years of age. -- Must be a high school graduate or currently attending high school. Necessary Knowledge, Skills and Abilities -- Outstanding aquatic skills and proficiency. -- Ability to demonstrate a pleasing personality and positive/assertive character traits. -- Ability to communicate effectively with children and adults. -- Ability to remain alert, attentive, and responsible. Additional Information: Wages: $16.80/hour Application Instructions: Please review the SUNY Child Protection Policy and complete the Policy Acknowledgment form to be uploaded along with resume: Child Protection Policy: https://www.suny.edu/sunypp/documents.cfm?doc_id=762 Policy Acknowledgment: https://www.delhi.edu/mydelhi/faculty-staff/administration/human_resources/pdf/Child Protection Policy Acknowledgement Form.pdf Fill out an Application.  (Be sure to save it to your computer using \"save as\") Upload your application, resume AND policy acknowledgement form when prompted **Please be sure your Adobe Acrobat software is up to date and that you are opening the application in Internet Explorer. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
