    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=141206": {
      "title": "SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Barnes & Noble Bookseller (Temporary)",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Barnes & Noble Bookseller (Temporary) SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Barnes & Noble Bookseller (Temporary) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Barnes & Noble Bookseller (Temporary) Category: Active Student Jobs Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Jan 5, 2022 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: PT No Benefits Position ID: 141206 Share About SUNY Delhi: Barnes & Noble College is a retail partner for nearly 800 colleges and universities nationwide.  We offer a retail environment like no other - uniquely focused on delivering essential educational content, tools, and merchandise within a dynamic retail environment on campuses of higher education.  Our teams interact directly with our customers including students, faculty, administration, alumni, and the general public to provide outstanding customer service to sell or rent books, general merchandise, and an array of products and services for an academic community all while being part of a company that is consistently rated as a great place to work - and where employees love what they do. Our stores can carry everything from text and trade books, technology, and school supplies to clothing, regalia, and food-- everything a college student desires, their parents want, and our faculty needs.  Temporary positions require availability to work on a weekly basis for a period of 90 days or less with occasional weekends, and flexibility in scheduling for opening, midday, or closing shifts. Job Description: Expectations: Greet customers, answer questions, and assist with the purchase of merchandise or services. Shelve, arrange, clean, and organize product or space within the store to maintain an appealing sales floor. Assist with processing sales transactions involving cash, credit, or financial aid payments. Temporary positions require availability to work on a weekly basis for a period of 90 days or less with occasional weekends, and flexibility in scheduling for opening, midday, or closing shifts. Physical Demands: Frequent movement within the store to access various departments, areas, and/or products. Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods. Frequent lifting. Occasional reaching, stooping, kneeling, crouching, and climbing ladders. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications Candidates must be a minimum of 18 years of age to be considered for employment. High-energy, friendly personality, with strong communication skills to interact with a variety of people. Outstanding customer service skills to match customers to products that meet their needs. Basic math, keyboarding, and data entry skills. Flexibility in scheduling is necessary. Preferred Behavioral Qualifications: Team Player: Works well as a member of a group Enthusiastic: Shows intense and eager enjoyment and interest Preferred Motivational Qualifications Self-Starter: Inspired to perform without outside help Flexibility: Inspired to perform well when granted the ability to set your own schedule and goals Additional Information: Barnes & Noble College is an Equal Employment Opportunity and Affirmative Action Employer committed to diversity in the workplace.  Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, gender identity, disability or protected veteran status. Application Instructions: To apply please complete this application. Bookseller application. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=197435": {
      "title": "SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Resnick Library - Library Student Assistant(s) Fall 2026",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Resnick Library - Library Student Assistant(s) Fall 2026 SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Resnick Library - Library Student Assistant(s) Fall 2026 Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Resnick Library - Library Student Assistant(s) Fall 2026 Category: Active Student Jobs Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Mar 16, 2026 Closes: Sep 18, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Part-time Temporary Ref. No.: RTF #343493 Position ID: 197435 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi has been delivering student-centered education in the foothills of the scenic Catskill Mountains for more than 100 years. A member of the State University of New York system, SUNY Delhi offers a supportive environment, and the chance to work among energetic colleagues and students on a friendly and inclusive campus. Job Description: Primary Responsibilities: Student manager of the library on weekends Open and close building on assigned days Assist library patrons in locating library materials, troubleshoot basic printing and software problems, check in/out library materials and equipment Assist with shelving library materials and other tasks as assigned Provide a conducive work environment for all students using the library Provide Leadership to fellow student workers Enforce appropriate library behavior, as needed *UPDATE as of August 25, 2026* Please note that we are primarily seeking students with weekend availability. Additional weekday hours are also available. Requirements: Cumulative College GPA of 3.0 Be in good judicial standing with the college Outstanding customer services skills Excellent interpersonal and communication skills Willingness to both supervise and enforce campus/library policy among peers Self-confident, self-directed using common sense and good judgment Strong computer skills and ability to learn new systems Preferred requirements: Completion of minimum 2 semesters on the SUNY Delhi campus (but freshmen are encouraged to apply) Reside on campus Additional Information: Library Hours: (covered by multiple students) Beginning of the semester Monday - Thursday: 8:00 am - 10:00 pm Friday: 8:00 am - 8:00 pm Saturday: 12:00 pm - 4:00 pm Sunday: 12:00 pm - 10:00 pm Beginning week 6 of the semester Monday - Thursday: 8:00 am - 12:00 am Friday: 8:00 am - 8:00 pm Saturday: 12:00 pm - 4:00 pm Sunday: 12:00 pm - 12:00 am *Additional hours as needed for special events and finals week Wages: $16.00 per hour Application Instructions: Fill out an Application .  (Be sure to save it to your computer using \"save as\") Upload your application AND resume when prompted **Please be sure your Adobe Acrobat software is up to date and that you are opening the application in Internet Explorer. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
